WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:04.240
This video shows how to install UM-Codex on a Mac.

00:04.240 --> 00:06.320
First, what to have ready.

00:06.320 --> 00:09.040
Then, the one command that installs it.

00:09.040 --> 00:12.320
Then, Docker Desktop and your key.

00:12.320 --> 00:14.360
And last, how to open UM-Codex.

00:15.560 --> 00:19.720
UM-Codex runs Codex in a sealed environment on your own computer.

00:19.720 --> 00:24.160
You need a Mac, your key for the University of Michigan's GPT Toolkit,

00:24.160 --> 00:25.740
which is in Aman's email,

00:25.740 --> 00:30.500
shared on Dropbox, and Docker Desktop, which runs the sealed environment.

00:30.500 --> 00:34.856
If Docker Desktop isn't installed, setup offers to install it.

00:36.056 --> 00:37.276
Open Terminal.

00:37.276 --> 00:41.116
Press Command and Space, type Terminal, and press Return.

00:41.116 --> 00:44.120
It's also in Applications, under Utilities.

00:44.620 --> 00:49.540
Paste the install command from UM-Codex's page on GitHub, and press Return.

00:49.540 --> 00:53.260
It works through six steps, and each one says what it's doing.

00:54.460 --> 00:56.700
Step one is Docker Desktop.

00:56.700 --> 00:59.340
On this Mac it's already installed and running.

00:59.340 --> 01:05.140
On a Mac without Docker, the installer asks first, then downloads and installs it.

01:05.640 --> 01:10.440
Steps two to four install UM-Codex itself, with its own copy of Python,

01:10.440 --> 01:12.820
and download the sealed environment's image.

01:12.820 --> 01:15.840
The download is the long part, the first time.

01:16.340 --> 01:18.400
Step five asks for your key.

01:18.400 --> 01:22.300
Copy it from Aman's email, paste it, and press Return.

01:22.300 --> 01:26.980
Each character shows as a star, and the key is saved in your Mac's Keychain.

01:26.980 --> 01:31.364
It never goes into the sealed environment, and it isn't kept in any file.

01:31.864 --> 01:37.384
Step six adds the UM-Codex app to Applications, and a shortcut to your Desktop.

01:37.384 --> 01:41.604
If you have the Codex app, setup may also ask one question about it.

01:41.604 --> 01:44.544
It gives the reason, and Return means yes.

01:44.544 --> 01:45.736
Then it's done.

01:46.936 --> 01:51.816
To open UM-Codex, double-click the UM-Codex icon on your Desktop.

01:51.816 --> 01:55.048
It's also in Applications, and Spotlight finds it.

01:55.548 --> 01:58.288
It opens UM-Codex's window in your browser.

01:58.288 --> 02:01.528
That's a page running on your own Mac, not a website.

02:01.528 --> 02:05.244
The line at the top says Docker is running and your key is saved.

02:05.744 --> 02:07.764
That's UM-Codex installed.

02:07.764 --> 02:12.200
In the next video, Your first launch, you start Codex in a folder.
